  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Tertiary butyl cyclohexyl ether on treatment with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HI</mi></math> forms tertiary butyl iodide and cyclohexanol.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mn>1</mn></math> mechanism is followed as the tertiary carbocation formed is stable.</p><p>The iodide nucleophile gets attached to the tertiary carbon atom to form tertiary butyl iodide and the cyclohexyl group that is connected to oxygen forms a bond with hydrogen coming from the dissociation of hydrogen iodide to form cyclohexanol.</p><p>The equation of the reaction is:</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/c7db7bfb-cf51-485c-aa99-f2488f441c93.png\" style=\"width: 750px; height: 343px;\"/></p><p>Hence, the answer is option D.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
